    {
     "id": "3da9d083-a0b3-4930-a020-7a94d54769dc",
     "prompt": "To factorise $6x^2+11x+3$ by splitting the middle term, which two numbers should be used?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "6 and 5",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "18 and $-7$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "9 and 2",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "3 and 6",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "The numbers must multiply to $6\\times3=18$ and add to 11. Since $9\\times2=18$ and $9+2=11$, split $11x$ into $9x+2x$."
    },
    {
     "id": "772a9764-4418-481e-bb52-5b4dbf02af1f",
     "prompt": "Factorise $6x^2+11x+3$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$(6x+1)(x+3)$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(3x+1)(2x+3)$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$(3x+3)(2x+1)$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(6x+3)(x+1)$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Splitting the middle term gives $6x^2+9x+2x+3$. Factorising by grouping produces $3x(2x+3)+1(2x+3)=(3x+1)(2x+3)$."
    },
    {
     "id": "5ac8a4db-6acb-4d82-96cd-dfab1952897c",
     "prompt": "Factorise $8x^2-2x-3$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$(4x+3)(2x-1)$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(8x+3)(x-1)$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(4x-1)(2x+3)$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(4x-3)(2x+1)$",
       "correct": true
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "The product $8\\times(-3)=-24$, so split $-2x$ as $4x-6x$. Grouping then gives $4x(2x+1)-3(2x+1)=(4x-3)(2x+1)$."
    },
    {
     "id": "9bdac9ba-632a-4e6c-b901-99bab0300379",
     "prompt": "Factorise fully $12x^2-75$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$3(2x-5)(2x+5)$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$3(4x^2-25)$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$3(4x-5)(x+5)$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$(6x-15)(2x+5)$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "First take out the common factor 3: $12x^2-75=3(4x^2-25)$. Then use the difference of two squares: $4x^2-25=(2x-5)(2x+5)$."
    },
    {
     "id": "2ec40b00-4a15-4777-9637-365b535c1f21",
     "prompt": "Solve $3x^2+x-2=0$ by factorising.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$x=-\\frac{2}{3}$ or $x=1$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$x=2$ or $x=-1$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$x=\\frac{2}{3}$ or $x=-1$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$x=-\\frac{1}{3}$ or $x=2$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "The quadratic factorises as $(3x-2)(x+1)=0$. Therefore $3x-2=0$ gives $x=\\frac{2}{3}$, while $x+1=0$ gives $x=-1$."
